  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Tensions have intensified between the Samajwadi Party and the Congress party regarding seat-sharing arrangements for the upcoming Uttar Pradesh assembly elections. Negotiations, which took place at the residence of senior Congress leader Pramod Tiwari in Delhi, concluded without a resolution. The conflict escalated after the Samajwadi Party publicly offered 26 seats to Congress, a proposal viewed by several Congress members as insufficient and premature. Prominent Congress figures, including Imran Masood and Rajendra Pal Gautam, have publicly criticized the move, with some members describing the unilateral announcement of candidates as undermining the spirit of alliance discussions. In response, sources within the Samajwadi Party indicated they felt compelled to make the announcement during the ongoing talks. The dispute continues to cause friction within the political coalition as both parties seek to align their strategies for the 2027 state elections while managing internal dissatisfaction over the negotiation process.",
